### 🖥️ Phase 1: Edge Mini PC Backend Deployment (Intel N100 + Hailo M.2)

#### 1. Hardware & Driver Setup on Host Ubuntu:
```bash
# 1. Update system packages
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# 2. Install Intel QuickSync VA-API drivers
sudo apt install -y intel-media-va-driver-non-free vainfo vainfo

# Verify hardware decode (/dev/dri/renderD128)
vainfo

# 3. Install HailoRT PCIe driver (for Hailo-8 M.2 module)
sudo dpkg -i hailort-pcie-driver_*.deb
sudo dpkg -i hailort_*.deb

# Verify Hailo chip detection (/dev/hailo0)
hailortcli scan
```

#### 2. Launch Stack with Docker Compose:
```bash
cd /home/meoclavezz/Projects-1/Edge_AI_CCTV/edge_backend

# Generate local SSL certs for HTTPS and WSS
python3 scripts/generate_certs.py

# Launch all 5 microservices (coturn, go2rtc, edge_api, caddy, tailscale)
docker compose up -d --build
```

#### 3. Enable Auto-Start on Boot via `systemd`:
Create `/etc/systemd/system/cctv-edge.service`:
```ini
[Unit]
Description=Edge AI CCTV Surveillance Stack
After=docker.service
Requires=docker.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=yes
WorkingDirectory=/home/meoclavezz/Projects-1/Edge_AI_CCTV/edge_backend
ExecStart=/usr/bin/docker compose up -d
ExecStop=/usr/bin/docker compose down
TimeoutStartSec=0

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```
Enable and start:
```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable cctv-edge.service
```

